--- !u!114 &-4607253924680453903
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Some CAD models do not include usable UV mapping, which is essential
      for applying textures and lighting correctly in Unity. The <b>Create UVs</b>
      action in the <b>Unity Asset Transformer Toolkit (UATT)</b> automatically generates
      UV coordinates during import, making the model ready for proper material rendering
      and lightmapping.

      In this step, you''ll add a new rule to generate UVs
      for the imported model.'
--- !u!114 &-4264417300288363221
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '1. In the <b>Import Rules</b> Rule Set, select <b>Add Rule</b>.


      2.
      Set the action type to <b>Run Rules</b>.


      3. In the <b>Run Rules</b>
      action, select the <b>Replace Materials on MetaData</b> Rule Set.


      4.
      Click the <b>plus (+) sign</b> to add another rule.


      5. Use the Radio
      button to select <b>Bake Ambien Occlusion</b> as the rule to run.


      6.
      Click the <b>plus (+) sign</b> again.


      7. Use the Radio button to select
      the <b>Add Lights</b> rule.'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-4066607638158195043
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "To make your CAD model interactive or usable in physics-based
      simulations, it needs colliders. Manually adding colliders to each part of
      a large model can be tedious. The <b>Create Colliders</b> action in the <b>Unity
      Asset Transformer Toolkit (UATT)</b> generates colliders automatically based
      on the geometry of the imported model.\nIn this step, you\u2019ll add a rule
      that applies colliders across the model during import."
--- !u!114 &-3642445344582918373
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this step, you\u2019ll open the Replace Material rule and
      configure it to search for specific metadata in a CAD model, then assign a
      new material to matching parts. This is a powerful way to automate repetitive
      editing tasks, such as assigning materials based on metadata tags."
--- !u!114 &-3535669443452494191
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You\u2019ve now created a basic AO baking rule that is  applied
      to the whole model during import. In the next step, you will extend this Rule
      Set to target specific parts of the model."
--- !u!114 &-3212019947421067349
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>RuleSets</b> folder, double-click the <b>Replace
      Material</b> Rule Set to open it if it is not already open.\n\n2. Select the
      <b>Three dot (\u22EE) menu</b> next to the rule name and select <b>Copy</b>.\n\n3.
      In the <b>Assets > RuleSets</b> folder, double-click the <b>Replace Materials
      on Metadata</b> Rule Set to open it.\n\n4. In the <b>Replace Materials on Metadata</b>
      editor, scroll to the bottom of the rules list.\n\n5. Under the last rule,
      select the <b>Add Rule</b> button.\n\n6. Select the <b>Three dot (\u22EE) menu</b>
      on this new ruleand select <b>Paste</b>. Your <b>Yellow_Metallic_powder_coat</b>
      rule is now added to this new Rule Set.\n\n7. Make sure the top level <b>Moto
      GameObject</b> is selected in the Hierarchy, then in the  <b>Replace Materials
      on Metadata</b> window <b>Run</b> the rule. All of your materials are now replaced
      with custom made Unity shaders."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-3106991618999041289
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In <b>Unity Asset Transformer Toolkit (ATT)</b>, you can reuse
      existing rules by copying them from one Rule Set and pasting them into another.
      This is useful when you want to apply the same actions across different import
      workflows without recreating each rule from scratch.\nIn this step, you\u2019ll
      copy the <b>Replace Material</b> rule and add it to an existing Rule Set."
--- !u!114 &-3028342289059139842
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'You would have to create a new step for each of the materials
      in the project. Due to time constraints we provide an existing rule that will
      replace the rest of the materials. In the next step you will see how you can
      add your rule to the existing one.


      Read more about the different filter
      options in the <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.industry.toolkit@3.2/manual/Actions/Autogenerated/Group_Filter.html">Documentation</a>
      for the Unity Asset Transformer Toolkit.'
