--- !u!114 &555981092726408254
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>RuleSets</b> folder, double-click the <b>Replace
      Material</b> Rule Set to open it.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Select the <b>Three dot (\u22EE)
      menu</b> next to its name and select <b>Copy</b>.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. In the <b>Assets
      > RuleSets</b> folder, double-click the <b>Replace Materials on Metadata</b>
      asset to open it.\r\n\r\n\r\n4. In the <b>Replace Materials on Metadata</b>
      editor, scroll to the bottom of the rules list.\r\n\r\n\r\n5. On the last rule,
      open the <b>three dots (\u22EE) menu</b> and select <b>Paste</b>.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe
      <b>Replace Material</b> rule is now added to the<b>Replace Materials on Metadata</b>
      Rule Set. This allows your import process to include automatic material replacement
      without duplicating setup steps.\r\n"
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &699668839402648121
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>Project</b> window, go to <b>Assets</b> >  <b>Rule
      Sets</b> and double-click the <b>Replace Material</b> asset. A new tab appears
      next to the <b>Inspector window</b>, showing the <b>Rule Sets Editor</b>. You\u2019ll
      see that a <b>Get</b> action is already present. This determines which objects
      the rule will apply to and will change depending on what is selected in the
      Hierarchy.\n\n2. In <b>Assets</b> > <b>3DModels</b>, locate the newly imported
      <b>Moto prefab</b> again and drag it into the <b>Hierarchy</b>. \n\n3. Reset
      the <b>Transform</b> again in the <b>Inspector window</b> to centre the prefab
      in the scene.\n\n4. In the <b>Hierarchy window</b>, select the <b>Moto prefab</b>.
      The <b>Get</b> action updates to show the source as <b>Moto (GameObject)</b>.\n\n5.
      In the <b>Rule Sets Editor</b>, select <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n6. Select <b>Filter
      > Filter on Metadata</b>.This action lets you filter imported CAD objects based
      on their metadata values.\n\n7. Under <b>Property Filter</b>, set the <b>Filter
      String</b> value to <b>MaterialName</b>.\n\n8. Under <b>Value Filter</b>, set
      the <b>Filter String</b> value to <b>Yellow_Metallic_powder_coat_01</b>.\n\n9.
      Activate the <b>Include Subhierarchy</b> option.\n\n10. Select <b>Add Action</b>
      again.\n\n11. Select <b>Set > Set Material</b>.\n\n12. In the new action, select
      the radio button next to the <b>Material</b> property field and  assign <b>Yellow_Metallic_powder_coat_01</b>.\n\n13.
      Select <b>Run</b> in the Rule Set tab. The rule searches through the child
      objects of the <b>Moto prefab</b>, finds those that match the specified metadata,
      and assigns the <b>Yellow_Metallic_powder_coat</b> material.\n\n14. Select
      the <b>Three dot (\u22EE) menu</b> next to the rule name and select <b>Rename</b>.
      Name it  <b>Yellow_Metallic_powder_coat</b>."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &1404201277660737661
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In addition to modifying and filtering imported models, Rule
      Sets can also add or replace prefabs at runtime. This is useful for building
      complex assembly tools or augmenting imported assets with extra components.
      In this step, you\u2019ll create a Rule Set that automatically adds a LightRig
      prefab to the robot, positioning it to simulate functional robot lights."
--- !u!114 &1657507016105008965
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>Project window</b>, go to <b>Assets > RuleSets</b>.\n\n2.
      Right-click and select <b>Create > Asset Transformer > Rule Set</b>.\n\n3.
      Name the new asset <b>Bake Ambient Occlusion</b>.\n\n4. Select <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n5.
      Search for and select <b>Bake Ambient Occlusion</b>.\n\n6. Set <b>Storage Method</b>
      to <b>Vertex Color</b>.\n\n7. Set <b>Samples</b> to 16.\n\n8. Set <b>Denoiser</b>
      to <b>Low</b>.\n\n9. Expand the <b>Advanced section</b> and activate the <b>Singularize
      Instances</b> option.\n\n10. Open the <b>three dots (\u22EE) menu</b> next
      to the rule name and select <b>Rename</b>.\n\n11. Name the rule <b>Bake Main
      Model</b>."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
