--- !u!114 &1919695986211397410
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>Import Rules</b> Rule Set, select <b>Add Rule</b>.\n\n2.
      A new rule appears at the end of the list.\n\n3. Open the <b>Three dot (\u22EE)
      menu</b> next to the new rule\u2019s name and select <b>Rename</b>.\n\n4. Name
      the rule <b>Create Colliders</b>.\n\n5. With <b>Create Colliders</b> selected,
      choose <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n6. Search for and select <b>Create Collider</b>
      from the action list.\n\n7. Set the strategy to <b>Retopology</b>.\n\n8. Set
      the <b>Mesh Quality</b> preset to <b>Low</b>"
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &1978816384736208793
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>Project</b> window, go to <b>Assets > 3DModels.</b>\n\n2.
      Select the <b>Moto</b> import asset (not the prefab or scene object).\n\n3.
      In the <b>Inspector window</b>, select the <b>Rule Engine</b> tab.\n\n4. In
      the <b>Rule Se</b>t select the radio button and then select <b>Import Rule</b>
      from the list of available Rule Sets.\n\n5. Select the <b>Model</b> tab in
      the <b>Inspector window.</b>\n\n6. Set <b>Mesh Quality</b> to <b>Medium</b>.\nThis
      setting enables automatic mesh decimation during import, so you don\u2019t
      need a separate decimation step in your rule.\n\n\n<b>Re-Import the model</b>\n\n7. 
      At the bottom of the <b>Inspector</b>, select  <b>Re-Import</b>.\n\n8. Unity
      will reimport the CAD asset and automatically apply all actions defined in
      your <b>Import Rule</b> Rule Set."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
