  Text:
    m_Untranslated: The rule is now set up to scan the model for objects tagged as
      <b>glider_support_assm</b> and then remove the holes in the model.
--- !u!114 &3406665437371970938
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. In the <b>Import Rules</b> Rule Set, select <b>Add Rule</b>.\n\n2.
      A new rule is added to the bottom of the list.\n\n3. Open the <b>Three dot
      (\u22EE) menu</b> next to the new rule\u2019s name and select <b>Rename</b>.\n\n4.
      Name the rule <b>Generate UVs</b>.\n\n5. With <b>Generate UVs</b> selected,
      choose <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n6. Search for and select <b>Create UVs</b> from
      the action list."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &3598068067356737144
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "As your Rule Sets become more complex, it\u2019s helpful to
      break them into smaller, reusable parts. The <b>Run Rules</b> action lets you
      trigger other Rule Sets from within your current one. This allows you to organize
      logic into manageable chunks while still building a master rule that handles
      everything during import.\nIn this step, you\u2019ll link previously created
      Rule Sets together by referencing them in a new master Rule Set."
--- !u!114 &4573188419241988244
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. Expand the <b>Moto GameObject</b> in the <b>Hierarchy</b>
      and notice that there is a  <b>lightPlaceHolder-1</b> GameObject</b>. This
      is a <b>placeholder GameObject</b> that was created by the CAD technician to
      represent the final object in Unity. This allows Unity developers and artists
      to collaborate efficiently with CAD teams and helps automate a standard asset
      integration workflow.\n\n2. In the <b>Project window</b>, go to <b>Assets >
      RuleSets</b>.\n\n3. Right-click in the folder and select <b>Create > Asset
      Transformer > Rule Set</b>.\n\n4. Name the new asset <b>Add Lights</b>.\n\n5.
      Open the three dots menu next to the rule name and select <b>Rename</b>.\n\n6.
      Name the rule <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n7. Select <b>Add Action</b>.\n\n8. Search
      for and select the <b>Filter on Name</b> action.\n\n9. Set the filter String
      to <b>lightPlaceHolder-1</b>. \n\n10. Select <b>Add Action</b>, search for
      and select <b>Replace by</b>. This action allows you to replace a specified
      object with another in Unity.\n\n11. In the <b>Replace by</b> action, select
      the <b>radio button</b> next to the <b>GameObject</b> field.\n\n12. Then, in
      the selector window choose Assets and search for and choose <b>LightRig_CAD</b>
      to assign it as the child prefab to add.\n\n13. Select <b>Add Action</b> again
      and search for and select <b>Set Transform</b>.\n\n14. Ensure <b>Referential
      is set to Self</b>.\n\n15. In the <b>Rotation</b> field, set the <b>Y value</b>
      to <b>-180</b>.\n\n16. <b>Run</b> the rule.\n\n17. Expand the <b>Moto GameObject</b>
      in the <b>Hierarchy</b> again and notice that now there is a <b>LightRig_CAD</b>
      where the <b>lightPlaceHolder-1</b> used to be.\n"
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &4945740985394573315
